+# Revision — run 01M230P8RGN6HWTR6PZ966Q3B1
+
+- status reviewed: succeeded
+- review: .fabro/reviews/develop/01M230P8RGN6HWTR6PZ966Q3B1.md
+- seeds filed: fabro-eb3f (planner step 4 journal fallback when goal carries no seed id); fabro-f5d7 (engine read-only run/automation state snapshot reachable from workspace); fabro-6997 (planner prompt fs_hide-glob-empty + rg -rn footgun one-liners); fabro-154c (reviewer prompt: pin ADR-0019 seed-spec-mandate rule)
+- basis: run 01M230P8RGN6HWTR6PZ966Q3B1, workflow version fdcab06ec2d4960a3fe766ddfcda5b5639105f463e9e6cb414f4c8e48485976f, commit 11017eb56dd3a2bc74357d3f7cc3a0bbcf13cdcf
+- revised_at_commit: 11017eb56dd3a2bc74357d3f7cc3a0bbcf13cdcf (ADR-0015: engine drift signal for later judgement)
+
+## Findings
+
+### 1. Develop planner step 4: fall back to the run journal when goal text carries no seed id
+- filed: fabro-eb3f (priority 1)
+- Change: add to `.fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/planner.md` step 4 the one-line fallback revisor Step 3.5 has — when a run's `goal` names no seed id, read it from `.fabro/journal/<run_id>.jsonl`.
+- Evidence: run's own `fabro_runs_list` output (event seq 41) shows all 10 develop goals are the identical generic string; the in-flight-PR guard matched nothing.
+- Effect: mid-flight skip guard functional in the ~15-min claim-to-PR window; prevents wasted overlapping run + duplicate PR (~15 min, ~$0.73 each).
+- Relation: prompt-side complement to open engine seed fabro-9372 (cross-referenced, not superseded).
+
+### 2. Engine: persist a read-only run/automation state snapshot reachable from the run workspace
+- filed: fabro-f5d7 (priority 2)
+- Change: engine-side (`fabro-store` / `fabro_runs_list`), persist per run a read-only `fabro ps -a --json`-style state dump, or extend the run projection with a status timeline, readable by implementers.
+- Evidence: implementer journal (implementer@1, seed fabro-91ff) could not reach runs/automation DB state for runs 01M22X67GYXC/01M22VF9PWJH; incident-citing seed forced a superset fix.
+- Effect: incident-citing seeds verifiable; fixes target the actual cause (incl. alternative fabro-ee5d) instead of the union of hypotheses.
+- Relation: complementary to fabro-5a25 and fabro-313c (cross-referenced).
+
+### 3. Develop planner prompt: two footgun one-liners — fs_hide glob returns empty, never `rg -rn`
+- filed: fabro-6997 (priority 2)
+- Change: two one-liners in `planner.md`: (a) glob on fs_hide paths returns EMPTY, not an error — go straight to shell for `.fabro/**`; (b) never `rg -rn`, `-r` replaces — use `-n`.
+- Evidence: events seq 46–47 (silently empty glob), seq 52–54 (wasted ls/rg round, incl. a `rg -rn` that was harmless only because `-l` discarded `-r`).
+- Effect: −2 tool calls, −1 LLM round per planner pass touching platform paths.
+- Relation: extends fabro-2eb6 to the planner; engine-side notice is open fabro-8296 (cross-referenced).
+
+### 4. Develop reviewer prompt: state whether a seed-spec mandate satisfies ADR-0019
+- filed: fabro-154c (priority 2)
+- Change: one line in `.fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/reviewer.md` pinning whether a seed-spec mandate counts as a recorded user decision for capability-delta verdicts.
+- Evidence: reviewer observation 2 adjudicated the revisor's `git fetch origin <base-branch>` credential-bridge path by judgment call.
+- Effect: identical capability-delta verdicts across reviewers instead of flips between false blocks and silent ratification.
